          %h2#structural_induction Structural induction
          %p The principle of structural induction on raw terms and types says that to prove something about all of them, it suffices to consider raw terms and types constructed according to each of the above clauses (i.e. consider all possible labels for the root of an abstract syntax tree), assuming as an inductive hypothesis that the desired statement holds of all subtrees. This is a basic property of an inductive type; if our metatheory is set-theoretic then it can be proven from the definition of well-founded tree.
          %p
            Similarly, there is a structural recursion principle for defining pairs of functions with domains
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi RawTm
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RawTm
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RawTy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RawTy
          %h2#equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            \-equivalence
          %p
            We want to identify raw terms and types that differ only according to a renaming of bound variables. However, in defining this inductively, we end up having to also rename
            %em free
            variables in the terms where the variables are bound. We do this all together by defining a relation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi ρ
                    %mi M
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \sim_\rho M'
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Raw
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\in Raw(V,s)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Raw
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M'\in Raw(V',s)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            is a bijection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\cong V'
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M'
            as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in V
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\in V'
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi ρ
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \sim_\rho y
                if and only if
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(x)=y
            %li
              %p
                For ordered sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,X'
                of the same cardinality, let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi X
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi:X\cong X'
                be the unique order-preserving bijection between them, and with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                      %mi j
                      %mo ⊲
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_j = \{x_k \mid j \lhd k \}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                      %mi j
                      %mo ⊲
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X'_j = \{x'_k \mid j \lhd k \}
                as before we have similarly
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ξ
                          %mi j
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi j
                        %mo ≅
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo ′
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi_j : X_j \cong X'_j
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "monospace"}
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ;
                      %mover
                        %mi M
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi ρ
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "monospace"}
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ;
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mi M
                          %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathtt{C}(X;\vec{M}) \sim_{\rho} \mathtt{C}(X';\vec{M'})
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi j
                      %msub
                        %mo ∼
                        %mrow
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo ∪
                          %msub
                            %mi ξ
                            %mi j
                      %mi M
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_j \sim_{\rho \cup \xi_j} M'_j
                for all
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %li
              %p
                In all other cases (e.g. one of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M'
                is a variable and the other is an operator, or they are distinct operators),
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %msub
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi ρ
                      %mi M
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\sim_\rho M'
                is false.
          %p It is easy to prove by induction that:
          %ul
            %li
              For any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Raw
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\in Raw(V,s)
              we have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %msub
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi id
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\sim_{id} M
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi ρ
                    %mi M
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\sim_\rho M'
              then
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo ′
                      %msub
                        %mo ∼
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ρ
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M' \sim_{\rho^{-1}} M
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi ρ
                    %mi M
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\sim_\rho M'
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo ′
                      %msub
                        %mo ∼
                        %mrow
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo ′
                      %mi M
                      %mo ″
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M' \sim_{\rho'} M''
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %msub
                        %mo ∼
                        %mrow
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi ρ
                      %mi M
                      %mo ″
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\sim_{\rho'\circ\rho} M''
          %p
            In particular, each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∼
                    %mi id
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim_{id}
            is an equivalence relation on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Raw
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Raw(V,s)
          %h2#weakening_exchange_and_contraction Weakening, exchange, and contraction
          %p
            For any function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma :V\to W
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Raw
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Raw
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Raw(V,s) \to Raw(W,s)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \mapsto M[\sigma]
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            is a subset inclusion, this is “weakening”: adding a new unused free variable. But to define weakening inductively, we will need to involve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M[\sigma]
            when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            is an injection that is not a subset inclusion, and it is no extra trouble to define it for any function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            at all.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=x\in V
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x[\sigma] = \sigma(x)
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mo =
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "monospace"}
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ;
                        %mover
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=\mathtt{C}(X;\vec{M})
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M[\sigma]
                to be “
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "monospace"}
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ;
                      %mover
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathtt{C}(X;\vec{N})
                ” where
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi M
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_j = M_j[\sigma]
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                may not be disjoint from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                (though it is disjoint from
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi W
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{[W]}
                that is disjoint from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                and an order-preserving bijection
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ξ
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo ≅
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi :X \cong X^{[W]}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ξ
                        %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi j
                      %mo ≅
                      %msubsup
                        %mi X
                        %mi j
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi W
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi_j:X_j \cong X^{[W]}_j
                be the restriction of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
                to the variables bound in argument
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi M
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi σ
                        %mo ∪
                        %msub
                          %mi ξ
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Raw
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mo ∪
                        %msubsup
                          %mi X
                          %mi j
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_j[\sigma\cup \xi_j] \in Raw(W\cup X^{[W]}_j,s_j)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi M
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi σ
                        %mo ∪
                        %msub
                          %mi ξ
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_j = M_j[\sigma\cup \xi_j]
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "monospace"}
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ;
                        %mover
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "monospace"}
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ;
                        %mover
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathtt{C}(X;\vec{M})[\sigma] = \mathtt{C}(X^{[W]};\vec{N})
          %p
            It is easy to prove by induction that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho,\rho'
            are bijections and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi σ
                    %mo =
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho' \circ \sigma = \sigma'\circ \rho
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mo ∼
                    %mi ρ
                  %mi M
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\sim_\rho M'
            implies
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo ′
                    %mi M
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M[\sigma] \sim_{\rho'} M'[\sigma']
            = succeed "-equivalence." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
          %h2#substitution Substitution
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Raw
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi tm
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N\in Raw(V,tm)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Raw
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\in Raw(V\cup \{x\},s)
            where
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\notin V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Raw
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M[N/x] \in Raw(V,s)
            by induction on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=x
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x[N/x] = N
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo =
                        %mi tm
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s=tm
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=y
                for some variable
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\in V
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y[N/x] = y
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mo =
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "monospace"}
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ;
                        %mover
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M = \mathtt{C}(X;\vec{M})
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                in each
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi M
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_j
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi M
                          %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Raw
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo ∪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo ∪
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_j \in Raw(V\cup \{x\} \cup X_j,s_j)
                = succeed "\u201D" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi M
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_j[N_j/x]
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Raw
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo ∪
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %mi tm
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_j \in Raw(V\cup X_j,tm)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Raw
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo ,
                        %mi tm
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N\in Raw(V,tm)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_j = N[\sigma_j]
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi V
                      %mo ∪
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_j:V\to V\cup X_j
                is the obvious inclusion. Then we can define
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_j = M_j[N[\sigma_j]/x]
                and hence
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "monospace"}
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ;
                        %mover
                          %mi P
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M[N/x] = \mathtt{C}(X;\vec{P})
          %p
            Note that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitution
            is automatically “capture-avoiding” because of our “strong scoping” and local Barendregt convention. Before we can write
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M[N/x]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            to have the same free variables (except for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            has), and no bound variables in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            can coincide with these free variables; thus no free variables in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            can get “captured” when it is substituted under binders in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            are not “given” with the same free variables, we need to explicitly weaken them first in order to substitute, and the definition of weakening was forced by strong scoping to rename all bound variables to keep them distinct from the newly added free ones; in particular, the bound variables in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            must get renamed to differ from any free variables in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %em bound
            variables in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            (using the weakening
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\sigma_j]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            under which they are substituted, ensuring that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M[N/x]
            still satisfies the Barendregt convention.
